        "First schema: namespace 'user', id 'Profile', source ../../schemas/user.schema.json",
        "Second schema: namespace 'app', id 'Config', source ../../schemas/app.schema.json",
        "Both use @xschemadev/arktype adapter",
        "Run xschema generate in that directory",
        "Commit generated web/examples/typescript/arktype/.xschema/xschema.gen.ts",
        "Generated file exports schemas with keys 'user:Profile' and 'app:Config'",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Used two config files (user.xschema.jsonc, app.xschema.jsonc) since xschema namespace is per-file. Generated output manually via adapter CLI since packages aren't on npm yet."
    },
    {
      "title": "Create Valibot example and generate",
      "description": "As a developer, I need Valibot generated code with multiple namespaces for Twoslash to import.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Create web/examples/typescript/valibot/xschema.jsonc with two schemas",
        "First schema: namespace 'user', id 'Profile', source ../../schemas/user.schema.json",
        "Second schema: namespace 'app', id 'Config', source ../../schemas/app.schema.json",
        "Both use @xschemadev/valibot adapter",
        "Run xschema generate in that directory",
        "Commit generated web/examples/typescript/valibot/.xschema/xschema.gen.ts",
        "Generated file exports schemas with keys 'user:Profile' and 'app:Config'",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Used two config files (user.xschema.jsonc, app.xschema.jsonc) since xschema namespace is per-file. Generated output manually via adapter CLI since packages aren't on npm yet."
    },
    {
      "title": "Install Twoslash packages",
      "description": "As a developer, I need fumadocs-twoslash installed to enable type hovers.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Run bun add fumadocs-twoslash twoslash in web/ directory",
        "Packages added to package.json",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "Configure Twoslash transformer in source.config.ts",
      "description": "As a developer, I need Twoslash transformer added to Shiki config.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Import transformerTwoslash from fumadocs-twoslash",
        "Import rehypeCodeDefaultOptions from fumadocs-core/mdx-plugins",
        "Add rehypeCodeOptions with transformers array including transformerTwoslash()",
        "Add langs array with js, jsx, ts, tsx",
        "Enable createFileSystemTypesCache() for performance",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Also added themes (github-light/github-dark) as required by RehypeCodeOptions type"
    },
    {
      "title": "Add Twoslash CSS and UI components",
      "description": "As a developer, I need Twoslash styles and components for type popups to render.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add @import 'fumadocs-twoslash/twoslash.css' to src/styles/app.css",
        "Import Twoslash components from fumadocs-twoslash/ui in src/routes/docs/$.tsx",
        "Spread Twoslash components into MDX components object",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "Configure Vite SSR externals for Twoslash",
      "description": "As a developer, I need typescript and twoslash externalized to avoid SSR bundling issues.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add ssr.external array to vite.config.ts with 'typescript' and 'twoslash'",
        "Typecheck passes",
        "Verify in browser using dev-browser skill - docs pages load without SSR errors"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "Add Twoslash to typescript.mdx client setup",
      "description": "As a user reading the TypeScript guide, I want to see types when using createXSchemaClient.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add twoslash to 'Use the client' code block (around line 92)",
        "Add ^? annotation under profileSchema variable to show its type",
        "Import uses relative path to examples/typescript/zod/.xschema/xschema.gen",
        "Typecheck passes",
        "Verify in browser using dev-browser skill - hovering shows Zod schema type"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Used virtual files pattern with // @filename: directives. Had to inline @xschemadev/client types since it's not published to npm. The ^? annotation shows ZodObject<{ id: ZodString; name: ZodOptional<ZodString>; email: ZodString }, $loose>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Add Twoslash to typescript.mdx schema lookup section",
      "description": "As a user, I want to see return types for schema lookups including multi-namespace and defaultNamespace.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add twoslash to 'Schema lookup' code blocks (around line 135)",
        "Show xschema('user:Profile') with ^? annotation showing Zod schema type",
        "Show xschema('app:Config') with ^? annotation showing different schema type",
        "Show defaultNamespace: 'user' example with shorthand xschema('Profile')",
        "Typecheck passes",
        "Verify in browser using dev-browser skill"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Added twoslash to both Schema lookup code blocks. First block shows full key format with types for both user:Profile (ZodObject with id, name?, email) and app:Config (ZodObject with theme enum, language, debug?). Second block shows defaultNamespace example with shorthand Profile lookup resolving correctly."
    },
    {
      "title": "Add Twoslash to typescript.mdx XSchemaType section",
      "description": "As a user, I want to see what types XSchemaType extracts.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add twoslash to XSchemaType example (around line 159)",
        "Add ^? annotation to show extracted type shape",
        "Add twoslash to function signatures example showing typed property access",
        "Typecheck passes",
        "Verify in browser using dev-browser skill"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "Add autocomplete and error examples to typescript.mdx",
      "description": "As a user, I want to see autocomplete for schema keys and errors for invalid keys so I understand the DX benefits.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add 'Developer Experience' or similar section to typescript.mdx after 'Using the Client'",
        "Show autocomplete example using ^| annotation displaying available schema keys",
        "Show error example using @errors annotation for invalid key like xschema('wrong:Key')",
        "Add Callout reminding users to run xschema generate after schema changes",
        "Typecheck passes",
        "Verify in browser using dev-browser skill - autocomplete popup and error highlight visible"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "notes": ""
